  "result": "Excellent! The bulk discount feature is working perfectly. Let me create a summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the bulk discount feature with comprehensive testing. Here's what was done:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **Created `bulkDiscount()` function in `src/totals.js`**:\n   - Returns 2.5% off the amount after the line's initial discount for qty \u2265 10\n   - Returns 0 for qty < 10\n   - Uses banker's rounding for precision\n\n2. **Updated `lineVAT()` function**:\n   - Now accounts for bulk discount in VAT calculation\n   - Formula: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount - bulkDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate%`\n\n3. **Updated `invoiceTotals()` function**:\n   - Includes bulk discount in the total discount field\n   - VAT is calculated on the amount after both regular and bulk discounts\n\n4. **Re-exported `bulkDiscount` from `src/invoices.js`** for backward compatibility\n\n### Test Coverage:\n\nAdded 14 new bulk discount tests covering:\n- No bulk discount for qty < 10\n- Correct 2.5% calculation for qty \u2265 10\n- Bulk discount applied after line discount\n- Multi-line invoices with mixed quantities\n- Interaction with VAT and vouchers\n- Edge cases and rounding\n\nUpdated 4 existing tests in `invoices.test.js` and `export.test.js` to reflect the new bulk discount behavior.\n\n### Test Results:\n- **All 402 tests pass** (55 in totals.test.js, 347 previously)\n- Backward compatibility maintained\n- Real-world calculations verified\n\nThe feature correctly applies an additional 2.5% discount to lines with 10+ units, applied after the initial discount, with VAT calculated on the final discounted amount.",
